{"event_type":"review","id":"267455b84a528b1793e4a0c9ef5a4f7bf8ec4757aec66d44c5a60415afd97661","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T18:49:06Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c41aefe4ee90fa194c9175de6e57996270f8a3733253e650eadac5f22dffe0c5","sha256":"c41aefe4ee90fa194c9175de6e57996270f8a3733253e650eadac5f22dffe0c5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0795123c5b3f314d61f75becb76a2467a539d389453d96b30cb75c83a59b666a","sha256":"0795123c5b3f314d61f75becb76a2467a539d389453d96b30cb75c83a59b666a"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a466f062d03b24f771ef275e0ee30347d198b60189eeaaecc5106c1573d7ccb0","sha256":"a466f062d03b24f771ef275e0ee30347d198b60189eeaaecc5106c1573d7ccb0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a011e0bb720532f6bc435642e19460f81141d4fa59ff5b5dad1dd3b325558b27","sha256":"a011e0bb720532f6bc435642e19460f81141d4fa59ff5b5dad1dd3b325558b27"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dc72b32c746817bfe4ed6b3834b59368fa4d6163ed44737bb86facac24520c18","sha256":"dc72b32c746817bfe4ed6b3834b59368fa4d6163ed44737bb86facac24520c18"}],"attempt_id":"f2ec11673a85ab71ab729f8335a4ce9e1f25fdcf36a26d540d24d58f178e00af:0:1","base":"ba2adbae8383ff1bf47b76af40afe2ddada557cc","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b059d51882b91b91cbff88d646435c9ef2a3e1f9","body":"**Non-canonical numeric tokens for numeric `run-plan` flags exit 2.**\n\nLine 203 keeps any numeric-looking token whose text differs from `String(Number(raw))` as a raw string (#386). That is correct for hex cluster ids. It also applies to ordinary numeric flags. For example, `--max-usd=0.50`, `--max-usd=5.0` and `--max-usd=2.00` all stay strings.\n\n`RunPlanInputSchema` then rejects them: `maxUsd` is `z.number()` and `maxTokens` is `z.number().int()`. A user who types a trailing-zero dollar cap gets `invalid input … expected number` with exit 2. The run does not start, so nothing runs unguarded. The cost is a confusing usage error on a common spelling.\n\nFix this in the `run-plan` schema, because only that schema knows these fields are numeric. Add a preprocess to `maxUsd`, `maxTokens` and `concurrency` in `src/cli/run-plan.ts` that converts a string matching `/^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/` with `Number(...)`. Op subcommands with numeric fields can use the same helper. Leave `parseFlags` unchanged.\n\n```ts\nconst numericFlag = (inner: z.ZodType<number>) =>\n  z.preprocess(\n    (v) => (typeof v === 'string' && /^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/.test(v) ? Number(v) : v),\n    inner,\n  );\n```","id":"2b9e7b1f7f69154b4d59bbb5bc6889f40bd45635dbb6cbcc1eae7805e2a07d31","intervals":[],"path":"src/cli/main.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Non-canonical numeric tokens for numeric `run-plan` flags exit 2."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"74a199bba441aa1504df9fa3584913158f94d597","body":"**Reject an existing session id in `create()`.**\n\n`create()` uses `appendFile` with the default `'a'` flag and has no existence check. If `requestedSessionId` names an existing `<id>.jsonl`, `create()` appends a second `session` header to that file. It then returns an empty record. The next `load()` throws `session: duplicate header at line N`, so the original session cannot be resumed. `create()` also reports success after it writes to the existing file.\n\nA leftover torn-header fragment has the same effect. `create()` does not run the torn-tail recovery that `appendMessage` runs. Its header is appended directly after the fragment, which can produce one malformed line.\n\nOpen the file with `flag: 'wx'`. A collision then fails with `EEXIST` and writes nothing. Map `EEXIST` to a clear error.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    await appendFile(this.pathFor(sessionId), `${JSON.stringify(line)}\\n`, {\n-      encoding: 'utf8',\n-      mode: 0o600,\n-    });\n+    try {\n+      await appendFile(this.pathFor(sessionId), `${JSON.stringify(line)}\\n`, {\n+        encoding: 'utf8',\n+        mode: 0o600,\n+        flag: 'wx',\n+      });\n+    } catch (err) {\n+      if ((err as { code?: unknown }).code === 'EEXIST') {\n+        throw new Error(`session: sessionId '${sessionId}' already exists`, { cause: err });\n+      }\n+      throw err;\n+    }\n```\n</details>","id":"52009a16f73f00163cbbb4965abfb07d9e3f0f5064d526356a82543bf410dd35","intervals":[],"path":"src/harness/session.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject an existing session id in `create()`."}],"head":"e93a96ccb7465dc3e2cd03ed4a009dfe0b36eff9","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"cfcf0a047f2947a0486047f5b7f5dda12c199270","intervals":[[1,77]],"path":"src/cli/README.md"},{"blob":"b059d51882b91b91cbff88d646435c9ef2a3e1f9","intervals":[[1,851]],"path":"src/cli/main.ts"},{"blob":"44fcc3fdd80743cebda238a5de8f5542ab963954","intervals":[[1,269]],"path":"src/cli/output.ts"},{"blob":"ef679b1b6641c5181eb061f26156f84317c3e2b6","intervals":[[1,531]],"path":"src/cli/run-plan.ts"},{"blob":"8e4171161f5a3983a37d2ea46490eb4daf86fe2d","intervals":[[1,193]],"path":"src/harness/config.ts"},{"blob":"74a199bba441aa1504df9fa3584913158f94d597","intervals":[[1,450]],"path":"src/harness/session.ts"},{"blob":"aea0e3eef00f31a677d31c0f1aac18997071012f","intervals":[[1,423]],"path":"src/index.ts"},{"blob":"ae68059e9d0b00b6b4110ace9c11f96e037dc50b","intervals":[[1,138]],"path":"src/ops/review/verifyReviewOutcome.ts"}],"job_id":"f2ec11673a85ab71ab729f8335a4ce9e1f25fdcf36a26d540d24d58f178e00af:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"ae68059e9d0b00b6b4110ace9c11f96e037dc50b","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/verifyRevie